# Environment
#
# Default-deny across the whole `.env` namespace, with the published template
# as the one exception. The previous rules named `.env`, `.env.local` and
# `.env.*.local` and nothing else, so a backup written beside the real file
# was not ignored and `git add -A` took it — which is how two copies of a
# working `.env` came to be committed and are now permanently in the history
# of every clone (GHSA-57rw-w33m-cp5v). Enumerating the backup spellings
# would have closed those two names; denying the namespace closes the next
# one too. `scripts/check_env_backup_files.py` holds both halves to it,
# because `.gitignore` has no effect on a file that is already tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

